Vacaturebeschrijving
   Are you looking for a stable job with fixed working hours and a reliable employer? Do you enjoy physical work and working together with colleagues? Then we have a great opportunity for you!
FunctieomschrijvingFor our client, we are looking for motivated Order Pickers to join a modern logistics team. Experience is welcome, but if you are motivated and willing to learn, we would also like to meet you.
As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse. Every day you make sure customer orders are picked correctly and prepared for delivery. Accuracy is important because customers depend on receiving the right products.
Your daily tasks include:
- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products for quality and quantity;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Making sure labels and orders are correct;
- Keeping your workplace clean, safe, and organised;
- Working together with your team to meet daily targets.

The work is active, so you'll be on your feet for most of the day. If you enjoy staying busy instead of sitting behind a desk, this job is a great fit.
Functie-eisenWe are looking for someone who:
- Speaks English, Polish and/or Dutch;
- Works accurately and pays attention to detail;
- Enjoys physical work;
- Can work independently as well as in a team;
- Is willing to work in a chilled warehouse environment;
- Is available to work Monday through Saturday. Working on Sundays and public holidays may also be part of the schedule;
- Has experience with order picking or a handheld scanner (preferred, but not required).

Arbeidsvoorwaarden- A starting salary of €2,600 gross per month (based on full-time employment);
- Shift allowance where applicable;
- Travel allowance;
- A good pension scheme;
- Stable working hours;
- A pleasant and international working environment;
- A reliable employer with long-term opportunities;
- The chance to develop yourself and grow within the company.

Bedrijfsomschrijving

As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse operation. Together with your colleagues, you make sure orders are processed efficiently and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Operating an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Checking products for accuracy and completeness;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace.

Thanks to a structured onboarding program, you'll quickly learn all aspects of the job.

- Are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Have a basic understanding of Dutch and/or English;
- Enjoy physical and active work;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Are motivated and eager to learn.

Previous logistics experience is a plus, but not required.

Are you detail-oriented, quality-focused, and looking for a full-time job in a dynamic logistics environment? Then this opportunity as a Quality Control Employee in Lelystad could be the perfect fit for you!

As a Quality Control Employee, you play a key role in ensuring that products meet the highest quality standards before moving further through the logistics process. You will work in a supportive team environment and be part of a 2-shift schedule (morning and afternoon shifts)

As a Quality Control Employee, your responsibilities include:

- Inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards;
- Identifying, reporting, and helping resolve product defects;
- Carefully checking products for damages, errors, or irregularities;
- Maintaining a clean and organized work area;
- Contributing to an efficient and high-quality logistics operation;
- Following quality and safety procedures at all times.

- Basic English communication skills are required;
- Full-time availability;
- Strong attention to detail and quality;
- Ability to work effectively in a team environment;
- Ability to follow instructions accurately;
- Previous experience in quality control, production, or logistics is an advantage, but not required.
